    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Siamese kingdom on an island in the Chao Phraya that dominated the central plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#thailand">Thailand</a> from 1351 to 1767.</li><li>Its wealth came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rice">rice</a> and royal trade, with Chinese, Japanese, Persian, Portuguese, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#dutch">Dutch</a> and French merchants living in the capital.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#burma">Burma</a> conquered it in 1569 and destroyed it in 1767, but its institutions passed to Thonburi and Bangkok.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1753 monks sent from Ayutthaya restored the full ordination of Buddhist monks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, founding the Siyam Nikaya, still the island's largest order.</p></aside>
    </section>

